WEBVTT

00:07.793 --> 00:09.034
- Are you ready, kids?
- 孩子们，你们准备好了吗？

00:09.103 --> 00:10.827
all:
Aye, aye, Captain!
全部：
是啊是啊，队长！

00:10.896 --> 00:12.206
- I can't hear you.
- 我听不到你说话。

00:12.275 --> 00:14.310
all:
Aye, aye, Captain!
全部：
是啊是啊，队长！

00:14.379 --> 00:17.275
- ♪ Ohh... ♪
- ♪ 哦...♪

00:17.344 --> 00:19.379
♪ Who lives in a pineapple
under the sea? ♪
♪ 谁住在菠萝里
在海底？ ♪

00:19.448 --> 00:21.379
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:21.448 --> 00:23.275
- ♪ Absorbent and yellow
and porous is he ♪
- ♪ 吸水性和黄色
他是多孔的 ♪

00:23.344 --> 00:24.965
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:25.034 --> 00:27.413
- ♪ If nautical nonsense
be something you wish ♪
- ♪ 如果航海废话
成为你想要的东西♪

00:27.482 --> 00:29.206
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:29.275 --> 00:31.344
- ♪ Then drop on the deck
and flop like a fish ♪
- ♪ 然后落在甲板上
然后像鱼一样扑通扑通♪

00:31.413 --> 00:33.379
all: SpongeBob SquarePants!
- Ready?
所有：海绵宝宝！
- 准备好？

00:33.448 --> 00:35.241
all:
SpongeBob SquarePants!
全部：
海绵宝宝！

00:35.310 --> 00:37.379
SpongeBob SquarePants!
海绵宝宝！

00:37.448 --> 00:39.482
SpongeBob SquarePants!
海绵宝宝！

00:39.551 --> 00:40.827
- SpongeBob
- 海绵宝宝

00:40.896 --> 00:42.689
SquarePants!
方裤！

00:42.758 --> 00:45.241
[laughing]
[笑]

00:45.310 --> 00:47.724
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

00:47.793 --> 00:49.379
[waves crashing]
[海浪拍打]

00:52.637 --> 00:55.568
[ukulele music]
[尤克里里音乐]

00:55.637 --> 01:02.155
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

01:02.224 --> 01:03.396
- Howdy neighbor.
- 邻居你好。

01:03.465 --> 01:05.844
It's your old pal Sandy Cheeks
这是你的老朋友桑迪·奇克斯

01:05.913 --> 01:09.568
with a true to life tale
direct from Bikini Bottom.
有一个真实的故事
直接从比基尼底部。

01:09.637 --> 01:12.155
It's the end of
another long day,
结束了
又是漫长的一天，

01:12.224 --> 01:16.051
and every critter in town is
getting ready to hit the hay.
镇上的每一个小动物都是
准备好上干草了。

01:16.120 --> 01:18.017
- [grunts]
- [咕哝]

01:18.086 --> 01:20.293
Whoo-hoo.
[snores]
呼呼。
[打鼾]

01:20.362 --> 01:22.775
- Even little old
SpongeBob and Gary
- 即使年纪不大
海绵宝宝和加里

01:22.844 --> 01:25.155
are laying down
their weary heads.
正在躺下
他们疲惫的头脑。

01:25.224 --> 01:26.948
- [grunts]
Night Gare-bear.
- [咕哝]
夜车熊。

01:27.017 --> 01:29.224
[yawns]
[哈欠]

01:29.293 --> 01:31.637
- Now snails love to sleep
- 现在蜗牛喜欢睡觉了

01:31.706 --> 01:34.603
but they also like
to have their fun.
但他们也喜欢
享受他们的乐趣。

01:34.672 --> 01:37.500
And clever little Gary
here is no different.
还有聪明的小加里
这里也不例外。

01:37.568 --> 01:38.775
[giggles]
[咯咯笑]

01:38.844 --> 01:41.155
With a dang nifty
decoy in place
非常俏皮
诱饵就位

01:41.224 --> 01:44.775
Gary is ready
to hit the town.
加里准备好了
去镇上。

01:44.844 --> 01:46.500
But first things first.
但首先要说的是。

01:46.568 --> 01:49.568
That gooey little
varmint is mighty hungry.
那个软乎乎的小
恶鼠非常饥饿。

01:49.637 --> 01:53.603
[chuckles] It may not
look like much to you and me
[笑]可能不会
对你我来说看起来很重要

01:53.672 --> 01:57.879
but this here is
four-star dining to a snail.
但这是
四星级的餐厅给了一只蜗牛。

01:57.948 --> 01:59.534
[laughs]
[笑]

02:01.637 --> 02:05.120
Now, Gary never minds
running into a friend
现在，加里不在乎
遇到一个朋友

02:05.189 --> 02:09.086
but old Patrick here don't
seem ready to share his meal.
但这里的老帕特里克不
似乎准备好分享他的饭菜了。

02:09.155 --> 02:11.051
- [growls]
- [yelps]
- [咆哮]
- [尖叫声]

02:11.120 --> 02:13.706
- [growling]
- [whimpering]
- [咆哮]
- [呜咽]

02:13.775 --> 02:16.775
- [barking]
- [吠叫]

02:16.844 --> 02:20.258
- [roaring]
- [咆哮]

02:20.982 --> 02:23.120
- [whimpering]
- [呜咽]

02:23.189 --> 02:27.465
- Ol' Gary feels as big as
a ten-point buck right now,
- 老加里感觉和
现在十块钱，

02:27.534 --> 02:29.500
but he's about to be reminded
但他即将被提醒

02:29.568 --> 02:31.775
that life ain't
all fun and games.
那生活不是
所有的乐趣和游戏。

02:31.844 --> 02:36.017
Especially when animal
control is on your tail.
尤其是当动物
控制权就在你的尾巴上。

02:36.086 --> 02:37.913
[exciting music]
[激动人心的音乐]

02:37.982 --> 02:41.189
- [grunting]
- [咕哝]

02:42.327 --> 02:44.017
Freeze, slime ball!
冻结，粘液球！

02:44.086 --> 02:46.706
- [meows]
- [喵]

02:46.775 --> 02:48.810
- Hmm?
[growls]
- 唔？
[咆哮]

02:48.879 --> 02:52.568
[warbling]
[颤音]

02:52.637 --> 02:54.982
[crash]
[碰撞]

02:55.051 --> 02:57.706
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

02:57.775 --> 02:59.120
[grunts]
[咕哝]

02:59.189 --> 03:01.120
[choking]
[窒息]

03:01.189 --> 03:02.810
[grunts]
[咕哝]

03:02.879 --> 03:06.534
- As much as Gary likes
getting one over on the heat
- 加里喜欢多少就多少
热度一过

03:06.603 --> 03:09.120
he has more important matters
to attend to.
他有更重要的事情
去参加。

03:09.189 --> 03:11.189
- [straining]
- [紧张]

03:11.258 --> 03:15.465
- This here is old Plankton's
restaurant, the Chum Bucket.
- 这是老浮游生物的
餐厅，Chum Bucket。

03:15.534 --> 03:17.568
Gary ain't here
for vittles, though.
加里不在这里
不过，为了维特。

03:17.637 --> 03:21.327
No one's ever at
the Chum Bucket for vittles.
从来没有人在
食物桶。

03:21.396 --> 03:23.155
[mischievous music]
[恶作剧的音乐]

03:23.224 --> 03:25.948
- [snoring]
- [打鼾]

03:26.017 --> 03:30.189
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

03:30.258 --> 03:34.224
[gurgling, coughing]
[咯咯声、咳嗽声]

03:34.982 --> 03:36.051
[snoring]
[打鼾]

03:36.120 --> 03:37.258
- [exhales]
- [呼气]

03:37.327 --> 03:39.706
- That there's spot.
- 有位置。

03:39.775 --> 03:42.603
Plankton's pet amoeba,
and Gary's best friend.
浮游生物的宠物阿米巴原虫，
和加里最好的朋友。

03:42.672 --> 03:44.017
- Psst.
- [barking]
- 嘘。
- [吠叫]

03:44.086 --> 03:45.913
- Spot's cute...
- 斑点很可爱...

03:45.982 --> 03:48.224
but about as dumb
as a barrel of hair.
但同样愚蠢
作为一桶头发。

03:48.293 --> 03:51.913
Gary better think quick
or they'll both be busted
加里最好快点思考
否则他们都会被抓

03:51.982 --> 03:54.362
before there
night's even begun.
在那之前
夜晚已经开始了。

03:54.431 --> 03:57.637
- [meows]
- [barking]
- [喵]
- [吠叫]

04:04.362 --> 04:07.258
- Ough.
- 哎呀。

04:07.327 --> 04:08.810
[snoring]
[打鼾]

04:10.362 --> 04:14.120
- Ol' Gary and Spot have
been sneaking out for ages
- Ol' Gary 和 Spot 有
已经偷偷溜出去好多年了

04:14.189 --> 04:16.396
though their owners
are none the wiser.
虽然他们的主人
没有人更明智。

04:16.465 --> 04:17.982
[both chattering]
[giggles]
[两人都在喋喋不休]
[咯咯笑]

04:18.051 --> 04:21.465
They love playing all
sorts of games together,
他们都喜欢玩
一起玩各种游戏，

04:21.534 --> 04:25.017
but their doggone favorite
is wrestling.
但他们最喜欢的
正在摔跤。

04:25.086 --> 04:28.327
[excited chatter]
[兴奋的喋喋不休]

04:30.017 --> 04:32.396
- It's the
Krusty Krab kitchen.
- 这是
蟹堡王厨房。

04:32.465 --> 04:34.189
- [meowing]
- What a stroke of luck.
- [喵喵叫]
- 真是太幸运了。

04:34.258 --> 04:37.293
Gary and Spot must have
worked up quite an appetite
加里和斯波必须有
胃口大开

04:37.362 --> 04:40.396
with all them fun and games.
充满乐趣和游戏。

04:40.465 --> 04:43.603
[accordion music]
[手风琴音乐]

04:43.672 --> 04:44.844
- [meows]
- [喵]

04:44.913 --> 04:47.844
- Uh oh.
That ice box is locked up
- 呃哦。
那个冰盒是锁着的

04:47.913 --> 04:50.844
tighter than a horse
thief in a hoosegow.
比马还紧
hoosegow 中的小偷。

04:50.913 --> 04:53.844
- [barking]
- [吠叫]

04:53.913 --> 04:59.086
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

04:59.155 --> 05:01.844
[panting]
[气喘吁吁]

05:01.913 --> 05:03.189
[yelps]
[尖叫声]

05:03.258 --> 05:04.948
[whines]
[哀鸣]

05:05.741 --> 05:08.913
- Oh boy.
It's chow time.
- 哦，孩子。
吃顿饭的时间到了

05:08.982 --> 05:10.258
- [yowls]
- [嚎叫]

05:10.327 --> 05:11.258
- [meows]
- [喵]

05:11.327 --> 05:13.775
[light music]
[轻音乐]

05:13.844 --> 05:14.948
- [barks]
- [吠叫]

05:15.017 --> 05:18.017
- [straining]
- [紧张]

05:19.465 --> 05:21.672
[SpongeBob laugh]
[海绵宝宝笑]

05:21.741 --> 05:23.051
- [barks]
- [吠叫]

05:23.120 --> 05:24.465
- [giggles]
- [咯咯笑]

05:24.534 --> 05:27.810
- [barking]
- [吠叫]

05:28.913 --> 05:30.120
- [humming]
- Whoo-whee.
- [嗡嗡声]
- 呼呼。

05:30.189 --> 05:32.982
Looks like Gary
is cooking up some fun.
看起来像加里
正在做饭一些乐趣。

05:33.051 --> 05:34.810
- [chattering]
- [喋喋不休]

05:34.879 --> 05:36.120
[bell dings]
[铃声]

05:36.189 --> 05:37.396
- [yelps]
- [尖叫声]

05:37.465 --> 05:40.637
- [chattering excitedly]
- [ barking]
- [兴奋地叽叽喳喳]
- [吠叫]

05:41.224 --> 05:42.844
- It may not be pretty
- 可能不太漂亮

05:42.913 --> 05:46.051
but to a critter,
chow is chow.
但对于一个小动物来说，
周就是周。

05:46.120 --> 05:53.362
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

05:56.327 --> 05:59.603
- [barking]
- [meowing]
- [吠叫]
- [喵喵叫]

05:59.672 --> 06:02.362
- Come out, come out.
- 出来吧，出来吧。

06:02.431 --> 06:05.051
[gasps]
Oh, there you are.
[喘气]
哦，你来了。

06:05.120 --> 06:07.258
[both chattering]
[两人都在喋喋不休]

06:07.327 --> 06:08.948
[dramatic music]
[戏剧音乐]

06:09.017 --> 06:10.155
- [whimpers]
- [呜咽]

06:10.224 --> 06:11.913
- [grunts]
Ow.
- [咕哝]
噢。

06:11.982 --> 06:13.224
[grunts]
[咕哝]

06:13.293 --> 06:16.982
Ha ha! I've got you this time.
哈哈！这次我有你了

06:17.051 --> 06:19.189
[warbling]
[颤音]

06:19.258 --> 06:20.465
[grunts]
[咕哝]

06:20.534 --> 06:22.362
[sad trombone music]
[悲伤的长号音乐]

06:22.431 --> 06:24.948
- Ahem.
- [grunts]
- 咳咳。
- [咕哝]

06:25.017 --> 06:28.948
Animal control, citizen.
I'm hunting an errant snail.
动物控制，公民。
我正在寻找一只迷路的蜗牛。

06:29.017 --> 06:31.534
- I don't give
a sea fig about snails.
- 我不给
关于蜗牛的海无花果。

06:31.603 --> 06:33.948
You tripped my silent alarm!
你触发了我的无声警报！

06:36.017 --> 06:37.775
Just look at this mess!
看看这烂摊子吧！

06:37.844 --> 06:39.982
Take that you varmint!
- [warbling]
就拿你这个恶棍来说吧！
- [颤音]

06:40.051 --> 06:41.189
- Take that!
- 拿着那个！

06:41.258 --> 06:42.913
[grunting]
- Ow! Ow! Ow!
[咕噜声]
- 噢！噢！噢！

06:42.982 --> 06:45.500
- [giggles]
Looks like our boys
- [咯咯笑]
看起来像我们的男孩

06:45.568 --> 06:47.948
gave Johnny law
the slip again.
给了约翰尼·劳
再次滑倒。

06:48.017 --> 06:52.396
Reckon they're gonna need some
place to lay low for a while.
估计他们需要一些
暂时低调的地方。

06:53.155 --> 06:54.051
- [both]
Phew.
- [两者]
唷。

06:54.120 --> 06:55.741
- Uh oh.
- 呃哦。

06:55.810 --> 06:59.844
Looks like their hiding
spot's all ready occupado.
看起来他们隐藏着
现场已准备就绪。

06:59.913 --> 07:02.155
Luckily for them,
Gary and Spot
对他们来说幸运的是，
加里和斯波特

07:02.224 --> 07:04.672
are all ready pals
with everyone here.
都准备好了朋友们
和这里的每个人。

07:04.741 --> 07:07.293
- Let's get this party started!
- 让我们开始这个派对吧！

07:07.362 --> 07:09.017
[grunts]
[咕哝]

07:10.982 --> 07:14.362
[dance music playing]
[all laughing and cheering]
[舞曲演奏]
[大家欢笑和欢呼]

07:14.431 --> 07:16.120
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

07:16.189 --> 07:17.810
- Uh oh.
- 呃哦。

07:17.879 --> 07:21.224
Looks like the fuzz
ain't gonna give up so easy.
看起来像毛茸茸的
不会那么容易放弃的

07:21.293 --> 07:24.189
- Hey, this is my Jam.
- 嘿，这是我的果酱。

07:24.258 --> 07:28.051
- They say that music
soothes the savage beast.
- 他们说音乐
安抚野蛮的野兽。

07:28.120 --> 07:30.051
- Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.
Oh, yeah.
- 哦，是的。哦，是的。
哦，是的。

07:30.120 --> 07:33.500
- But sometimes it works
on knuckle heads too.
- 但有时它会起作用
指节头上也有。

07:33.568 --> 07:34.775
- That's how you do it.
- 你就是这样做的。

07:34.844 --> 07:36.948
You do it.
You do it.
你做吧。
你做吧。

07:37.017 --> 07:38.568
[warbles, grunts]
[颤音，咕噜声]

07:38.637 --> 07:40.913
[record scratches,
glass shatters]
[记录划痕，
玻璃碎裂]

07:41.637 --> 07:44.844
Uh, you animals
are under arrest.
呃，你们这些动物
已被捕。

07:44.913 --> 07:46.465
[all growling]
Uh...
[全都咆哮]
呃...

07:46.534 --> 07:48.396
Uh oh.
[all grunting]
呃哦。
[全都咕哝]

07:48.465 --> 07:50.844
- Youch.
That's gotta hurt.
- 尤奇。
那一定很痛吧

07:50.913 --> 07:53.431
Oh mama.
哦妈妈。

07:53.500 --> 07:55.637
[both whimpering]
[两人都呜咽]

07:55.706 --> 07:58.362
[playful music]
[俏皮的音乐]

07:58.431 --> 08:00.362
[all growling]
[全都咆哮]

08:00.431 --> 08:02.258
- [strains, grunts]
- [紧张，咕哝声]

08:02.327 --> 08:03.500
[all grunt]
[全都咕哝]

08:03.568 --> 08:05.155
- [yawns]
- [哈欠]

08:05.224 --> 08:06.879
[grunts, hums]
[咕哝声，哼哼声]

08:06.948 --> 08:10.775
- I guess this party
just got pooped.
- 我猜这个派对
刚刚拉屎了。

08:10.844 --> 08:12.431
[ominous tone]
[不祥的语气]

08:12.500 --> 08:13.844
- [crying]
- Luckily,
- [哭泣]
- 幸运的是，

08:13.913 --> 08:15.603
SpongeBob's little Gare-Bear
海绵宝宝的小车站熊

08:15.672 --> 08:19.258
always has something
under his shell.
总是有一些东西
在他的壳下。

08:22.603 --> 08:24.017
- [meows]
- [喵]

08:24.086 --> 08:26.293
- Locked doors
are never a problem
- 锁着的门
从来都不是问题

08:26.362 --> 08:28.189
for a snail like Gary.
对于像加里这样的蜗牛。

08:28.258 --> 08:29.465
- [spits]
- [吐口水]

08:29.534 --> 08:31.775
- [grunts, squeaks]
- [咕哝声，吱吱声]

08:31.844 --> 08:35.086
[mischievous music]
[恶作剧的音乐]

08:35.155 --> 08:37.500
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

08:37.568 --> 08:40.120
[suspenseful music]
[悬疑音乐]

08:40.189 --> 08:42.810
- Now to most animals
the pound is scarier
- 现在对大多数动物来说
英镑更可怕

08:42.879 --> 08:44.948
than a bob cat
in your long johns.
比鲍勃猫
在你的长裤里。

08:45.017 --> 08:48.431
But Gary and Spot our on a
mission to save their pals.
但是加里和斯波我们在
拯救他们的朋友的使命。

08:48.500 --> 08:51.534
[both grunting, straining]
[两人都咕哝着，紧张着]

08:51.603 --> 08:55.293
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

08:55.362 --> 08:56.948
- [groans]
- [呻吟]

08:57.672 --> 08:59.017
- Aha!
- 啊哈！

08:59.086 --> 09:00.500
[exciting music]
[激动人心的音乐]

09:00.568 --> 09:02.534
- [yips]
- [哎呀]

09:02.603 --> 09:04.706
[squeaks]
[吱吱声]

09:04.775 --> 09:06.293
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

09:06.362 --> 09:08.327
all: Huh?
全体：啊？

09:08.396 --> 09:11.568
[all cheering]
[大家欢呼]

09:12.258 --> 09:14.120
- [meows softly]
Shh.
- [轻声喵喵叫]
嘘。

09:14.189 --> 09:15.396
[all grunt]
[全都咕哝]

09:15.465 --> 09:17.017
[tense music]
[紧张的音乐]

09:17.086 --> 09:18.086
- Hmm?
- 唔？

09:18.155 --> 09:19.775
- Oh, Marvin,
- 哦，马文，

09:19.844 --> 09:22.672
you could catch every snail
in Bikini Bottom
你可以抓住每只蜗牛
比基尼下装

09:22.741 --> 09:25.396
but the only thing
you've really caught
但唯一的事情
你真的抓住了

09:25.465 --> 09:27.327
is loneliness.
是孤独。

09:27.396 --> 09:29.534
[sobbing]
[抽泣]

09:29.603 --> 09:30.637
[coughing]
[咳嗽]

09:30.706 --> 09:32.189
And kennel cough.
还有犬窝咳。

09:32.258 --> 09:35.500
- Marvin here ain't
kith nor kin to Gary
- 马文不在这里
加里的亲戚

09:35.568 --> 09:37.258
but that don't matter none.
但这并不重要。

09:37.327 --> 09:40.672
Gary could never bear
to see anyone looking so down.
加里永远无法忍受
看到有人如此低落。

09:40.741 --> 09:43.396
- I need another snot rag.
- 我需要另一块鼻涕抹布。

09:43.465 --> 09:44.672
[somber ukulele music]
[忧郁的尤克里里音乐]

09:44.741 --> 09:47.431
- [meowing]
- [喵喵叫]

09:47.500 --> 09:48.844
[all grunt]
[全都咕哝]

09:48.913 --> 09:50.051
- [sobs]
- [抽泣]

09:51.224 --> 09:54.293
Hey!
How did you animals get out?
嘿！
你们这些动物是怎么逃出来的？

09:54.362 --> 09:57.120
[soft music]
[轻音乐]

09:57.189 --> 10:00.051
Wh-wh-what's going on?
什、什、这是怎么回事？

10:00.120 --> 10:05.189
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

10:05.258 --> 10:07.396
- Viola.
- 维奥拉。

10:07.465 --> 10:10.120
[grinding]
[研磨]

10:10.189 --> 10:12.017
[exhales, giggles]
[呼气，咯咯笑]

10:15.741 --> 10:19.672
- [gasps]
She's beautiful.
- [喘气]
她很漂亮。

10:19.741 --> 10:22.017
[sighs]
[叹气]

10:22.086 --> 10:24.775
[laughs]
[笑]

10:24.844 --> 10:26.362
[excited shouting]
[兴奋的喊叫]

10:26.431 --> 10:29.086
[both grumbling]
[两人都抱怨]

10:29.155 --> 10:32.396
[light music]
[轻音乐]

10:32.465 --> 10:35.672
- Oh!
That's so good!
- 哦！
那太好了！

10:36.775 --> 10:39.120
[sighs]
[叹气]

10:39.189 --> 10:40.534
[organ music]
[管风琴音乐]

10:40.603 --> 10:42.327
I do.
我愿意。

10:42.396 --> 10:45.086
[kissing]
[all cheering]
[接吻]
[大家欢呼]

10:45.155 --> 10:47.844
- [laughs goofily]
- [傻笑]

10:47.913 --> 10:50.051
I can't thank you all enough.
我对你们感激不尽。

10:50.120 --> 10:53.500
You brought love
into my lonely life.
你带来了爱
走进我孤独的生活。

10:53.568 --> 10:55.672
Everybody's free to go.
大家都可以自由活动了

10:55.741 --> 10:57.396
[cheering]
[欢呼]

10:57.465 --> 10:59.362
- [laughing]
Why am I running?
- [笑]
我为什么要跑步？

10:59.431 --> 11:01.120
- With their friends rescued,
- 他们的朋友获救后，

11:01.189 --> 11:04.879
it's time for our boys
to finally get some shut eye.
现在是我们男孩的时间了
终于可以闭上眼睛了。

11:04.948 --> 11:06.431
[light music]
[轻音乐]

11:06.500 --> 11:09.741
- [grunting]
- [咕哝]

11:09.810 --> 11:11.672
[barks]
[吠叫]

11:11.741 --> 11:15.431
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

11:15.500 --> 11:18.189
- [grumbling]
- [抱怨]

11:18.258 --> 11:20.155
- [meows]
- [喵]

11:20.224 --> 11:22.879
- After his long night
of adventuring
- 在漫长的一夜之后
冒险的

11:22.948 --> 11:26.051
Gary is more tired than
a bronco on busting day.
加里比他更累
野马在破坏日。

11:26.120 --> 11:28.293
[fog horn]
[雾号]

11:28.362 --> 11:30.948
- [gasps]
Come on Gary, you lazybones.
- [喘气]
来吧，加里，你们这些懒骨头。

11:31.017 --> 11:33.534
It's time to wake up.
是时候醒来了。

11:33.603 --> 11:35.948
- [yawns]
- [哈欠]

11:36.017 --> 11:39.741
- Oh well, maybe a few
more minutes wouldn't hurt.
- 哦，好吧，也许有一些
再多几分钟也没什么坏处。

11:39.810 --> 11:42.189
- Well, that's
the long and short of it.
- 嗯，那就是
它的长和短。

11:42.258 --> 11:45.224
See ya'll next time
for more true to life tales
下次见
更多贴近生活的故事

11:45.293 --> 11:46.603
of Bikini Bottom.
的比基尼底部。

11:46.672 --> 11:49.362
- Shhh.
- [growls]
- 嘘。
- [咆哮]

11:51.637 --> 11:54.568
[placid ukulele music]
[平静的尤克里里音乐]

11:54.637 --> 12:01.844
♪ ♪
♪ ♪

♪ ♪